{
  "_comment": "Permission contract for an eutropia session on commonwealth-ai (recipes/harness/claude reads this before ralph/claude-settings.json). Made 2026-10-23 from ralph/claude-settings.json for the engine-swap queue, which runs under eutropia on a Mac and on the Halo (inside the sovereign-vulkan toolbox). Changed from ralph's: the result verb is `eutropia result`, not ralph-result (a session that cannot reach its result verb is how eutropia's first real use failed, design D14); ralph-mark.sh is gone (the loop marks rows, a worker never does); `toolbox run -c sovereign-vulkan` is gone (a host-only command: on the Halo the session already runs inside the toolbox, and the Mac has none) and `flatpak-spawn --host podman` takes its place for the container builds the addendum sends to the host; the queue's declared checks resolve through `RALPH_QUEUE=engine-swap scripts/ralph-check.sh <check>` (eutropia exports no RALPH_QUEUE); `git merge origin/ralp/es-*` is the START FROM merge of a parked ralph lane; `shasum` is macOS's sha256sum. Kept from ralph's: defaultMode auto, every check command, the read-only shell, and the deny list (no push, no --no-verify, no history rewrite, no staging everything, no delegation, no web). LSP stays off (enabledPlugins + deny, a384d764f): lspmux starts one rust-analyzer per workspace root, so each lane cost its own 9-12 GB analyzer that no memory floor counted (2026-10-12: 3 GB available, swap full, at 3 lanes).",
